@* What a button leads with, and the ring it becomes while its action is in flight: a save, a
   send, a completed game.

   Six primary buttons in the app act on the server and hold a flag while they wait, and only two
   of them said so — Settings had grown a private <c>SaveGlyph</c> helper for its own pair, with a
   comment about the drift a second copy invites, and the four elsewhere (the setup form's two
   saves, the game page's "Save result", the first-login name prompt) went quiet instead: the
   button dimmed and nothing else happened until the page moved. On a slow save that reads as a
   click that missed.

   The ring is LoadingSpinner's inline form, which is drawn in white on white — right on the
   filled button every one of these is, and wrong on a .btn-secondary. Keep it to the filled ones,
   as they all are today. *@

@if (Busy)
{
    <LoadingSpinner Inline="true" Label="@BusyLabel"/>
}
else
{
    <Icon Name="@Icon" Class="w-4 h-4"/>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The glyph while the button is idle — what kind of act this is.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Icon { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>The action is in flight: the glyph becomes the ring.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Busy { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What a screen reader is told is happening while it spins.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string BusyLabel { get; set; } = "Saving";
}
